Linux Automation Monitoring, Cleanup, Logging & Auditing
The Problem
Managing Linux servers was becoming time-consuming.
I had to check CPU, memory, disk usage, processes, Docker resources, and EBS volumes separately.
Doing these checks manually takes time and makes regular cleanup harder to manage.
My Debugging Steps
• Checked CPU, memory, and disk usage
• Checked running processes
• Checked Docker resources
• Checked EBS volumes
• Looked for a simple way to automate these checks
The Solution
I built a Python automation script to bring these routine tasks into one place.
It supports Auto, Interactive, and Dry-Run modes so cleanup actions can be controlled safely.
I also added logging and audit records to track important actions.

Monitor → Detect → Decide → Cleanup → Log → Audit
The goal was simple: make Linux monitoring and cleanup easier, safer, and easier to track.
